#implementation
- implement a token parser for human.skills
- implementation is in typescript
- [path][line] numbers are targets and get updated after coding.
- $Linter, $GoToDefinition and $Highlighter work on *.bot as well as *.human

#vscode deployment
- package as a .vsix, installed with code --install-extension
- bundle the server and client with esbuild into vscode/dist
- the server runs on the node that comes with vscode
- publisher is benjit87
- published to the marketplace

@Data
- *.human file
- *.bot file // same syntax as human

@Structure
- - // a leading - marks a child of the previous header, bullet and indent, unlimited depth
- indent is 2 space only, error if its not

@Token
- @
- $
- ?
- //
- #
- ->
- +
- word // can represent methods or a defined behavior or just a sentence, semantically driven
- comment_sentence // the words after // , this represent instructions or remarks
- ==
- -
- word // a // inside quotes e.g "//" is a word, not a comment

@Node
- @Token // the token of this line
- children // @Node list, defined by - bullets and indent

@Tokens
- @Token // list

?Data
- @Data

?Parsed
- AST of @Node // tree of nodes, one per line

$Parser
- @Data -> tokenize -> @Tokens
- @Tokens + @Structure -> parser -> ?Parsed

$GoToDefinition
- define for me
- single .human file plus its sibling *.bot only
- on a definition header of @,$,? go to the same header in the *.bot
- if no *.bot or header, stay on the definition

$Highlighter
- @Token -> colour -> editor
- @
- $
- ?
- #
- "//"
- ->
- +
- ==
- -
- each get a colour

$Linter
- define for me
- unused-definition is a warning
- missing-robot only checked when file info is passed
- [path][line] target must exist, warning if the file or line is missing
- [path] is relative to the folder that holds .git or SKILLS.md
- missing-human, same as missing-robot, for *.bot

$LSP
- $GoToDefinition
- $Linter

$CLI
- cli def supports both name form and position form
- $GoToDefinition
- $Linter
